            <ArticleTitle>[Percutaneous cervical cordotomy in intractable cancer pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2650-1</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Percutaneous cordotomy by the lateral high cervical approach may be indicated in the treatment of intractable nociceptive or neuropathic cancer pain below the C5 dermatome. A description of the technique and two case studies are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
